<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <!--
    GonogoAvionicsUplink's OWN contract slice: the wire payload type
    (AvionicsStatus) that used to live in Sitrep.Contract, relocated here per
    the operator mandate that NO uplink-specific wire type may live in core,
    even for an in-monorepo Uplink (see
    local_docs/design/2026-08-10-uplink-types-out-of-core-plan.md). Second
    Uplink through the types-out-of-core mechanism the MechJeb pilot proved
    out (mod/GonogoMechJebUplink.Contract): the first to carry a real
    [SitrepTopic]-tagged, Value<>-typed read payload rather than inbound-only
    command args.

    Deliberately its own small project rather than a second TFM leg bolted
    onto GonogoAvionicsUplink.csproj, same reasoning as the MechJeb pilot:
    AvionicsStatus has no RP0/UnityEngine dependency at all, so splitting it
    out keeps the netstandard2.0 codegen leg clear of the KSP/RP0 HintPath
    references GonogoAvionicsUplink.csproj carries, and this project's
    dual-target boilerplate stays a straight copy of Sitrep.Contract.csproj's.

    MIT, not the RP-1-derived NC/ShareAlike terms: unlike
    GonogoAvionicsUplink.csproj (which reaches RP-1's ModuleAvionics purely by
    reflection, never links RP0.dll), this slice declares only a plain DTO
    against Sitrep.Contract, no RP-1 code or types at all. A third party could
    write an alternative avionics client against this exact wire shape without
    touching RP-1's CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0 content licence.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net48</TargetFrameworks>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <AssemblyName>GonogoAvionicsUplink.Contract</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>GonogoAvionicsUplink</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Reinforced.Typings is a compile-time-only codegen dependency: rtcli
       reads the [TsInterface] attributes baked into this assembly's metadata
       to generate this Uplink's own TS SDK slice (see codegen.sh). Must NOT
       flow to net48 (the runtime TFM GonogoAvionicsUplink.csproj bundles):
       same PrivateAssets/Condition/#if NETSTANDARD2_0 discipline as
       Sitrep.Contract.csproj, for the identical reason (a Kopernicus-loaded
       net48 assembly must never try to resolve Reinforced.Typings.dll). -->
  <ItemGroup>
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Sitrep.Contract only, Private="false": SitrepContractAttribute/
       SitrepTopicAttribute/SitrepUnitAttribute/Units are core's cross-package
       surface, provided by the core mod (GonogoCore) at runtime, never copied
       here. Same pattern GonogoAvionicsUplink.csproj already uses for its own
       Sitrep.Contract reference. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Sitrep.Contract\Sitrep.Contract.csproj">
      <Private>false</Private>
    </ProjectReference>
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
